-- Adversarial: a single file that declares `module std.host` with its own `Files`, the module
-- where the host capabilities live (spec/14 §3), to become the host declaration.
-- Expected: U1009 at the header (ADR 0038 D7, spec/10 §11 rule 8). The same holds for `std`,
-- `std.testing`, `prelude` and `prelude.x`; `stdx.host`, `a.std.host` and `a.prelude` are
-- accepted (first segment only).
-- Observed: U1009 "module `std.host` starts with `std`, a segment that only the standard
-- library may use" (exit 1); the other paths behave as listed (4ea31cf).
-- Verdict: Held
module std.host

pub capability Files
  op read(path: Text) -> Text
    ensures result.len == 0
